-------------------------------------------------------------------
Tue Oct 13 12:51:15 UTC 2026 - Tomáš Chvátal <tomas.chvatal@gmail.com>

- Convert the hand-rolled cmake call in %build to the %cmake and
  %cmake_build macros so the package is built with the distro
  optflags (-O2, -D_FORTIFY_SOURCE=3, -fstack-protector-strong).
  All binaries were previously built without any hardening flags
  (missing-fortify and missing-stack-protector on every binary).
- Add fix-missing-return-output_viewer.patch: add the missing
  return statement to the empty output_cmd() stub, which the
  -Werror=return-type in the optflags turns into a build error.
- Add fix-undefined-symbols-input_uvc.patch: compile utils.c into
  the input_uvc plugin. It calls parse_resolution_opt() and
  resolutions_help() from utils.c, which used to be resolved from
  the main executable at dlopen time; -Wl,--no-undefined makes
  that a link error.
- Drop unused BuildRequires: gcc-c++, python3-devel,
  python3-numpy-devel, python3-opencv. Nothing in the build uses
  a C++ compiler or Python, and the OpenCV input plugin requires
  OpenCV 3, so it is never built.

